bbcode_enabled = true
bbcode_text = "[center][color=yellow]--Dialogue Overview--[/color][/center]
The dialogue system has many components
and features to it to make it as versatile to 
use as possible. This page explains what each
object and property does. You'll find every 
object here in the [color=aqua]Entities[/color] category.

[center][color=yellow]--Dialogue Triggers--[/color][/center]
A dialogue trigger is used to add text boxes and NPC style text to a level. 
These can be placed anywhere you like. Like most objects, these have 
properties that you can tweak and customize to your heart's content;
[indent]
[color=#54f954]Dialogue[/color] - the text a dialogue trigger will use when actively talking with it.
 It is worth noting that this property is modified in a submenu. 
A quick description of what every button does:
[indent]
[color=aqua]Remove[/color] - Removes the last page from the dialogue
[color=aqua]Add[/color] - Adds a page to the end of the dialogue
[color=aqua]Switch to[/color] - ID of the dialogue object to switch to when finishing the page
[color=aqua]Expressions[/color] - click the head to cycle through the expressions (NPCs only)
[color=aqua]Actions[/color] - click the body to cycle through actions to perform 
on that page of dialogue (NPCs only)
[color=aqua]Responses[/color] - click Mario to cycle through reactions for the player 
to display after that page of dialogue
[/indent]
[color=#54f954]Bubble Text[/color] - text that appears overhead when the player is nearby
[color=#54f954]Tag[/color] - ID of this dialogue object, similar to water/lava
[color=#54f954]Delegate Tag[/color] - Will start dialogue from the specified object ID instead
[color=#54f954]Zoom[/color] - Will specify the zoom amount when focused on the object
[/indent]
[center][color=yellow]--NPCs--[/color][/center]
NPCs are objects specifically designed
for dialogue objects. When dialogue is 
placed on top of them, the dialogue will
attach itself to the NPC when playing.
Their properties are as follows;
[indent]
[color=#54f954]Idle Expression/Action[/color] - expression/action when idling
[color=#54f954]Speaking Expression/Action[color=red]*[/color][/color] - action when idling/speaking 
[color=#54f954]Tag Link[/color] - links a dialogue trigger to the NPC from a distance (uses Tag)
[color=#54f954]Path Options[/color] - properties like custom path, walk speed, physics enabled, 
and move type. Each are fairly self explanatory.
[color=#54f954]Path Reference[/color] - Gives a visual on where the NPC's path is located
[/indent][color=red]*require an attached dialogue trigger with bubble text[/color]

[center][color=yellow]--Signs--[/color][/center]
Signs act as single page NPCs that
cannot show emotion. These are best
used as, well, signs. There's nothing
very noteworthy to bring up
so properties won't be discussed here,
as they're self explanatory.

If anything above isn't clear or you still have questions, 
feel free to ask in the [url=https://discord.gg/QrftDjD][color=fuchsia]Super Mario 127 Discord[/color][/url]!
"
text = "--Dialogue Overview--
The dialogue system has many components
and features to it to make it as versatile to 
use as possible. This page explains what each
object and property does. You'll find every 
object here in the Entities category.

--Dialogue Triggers--
A dialogue trigger is used to add text boxes and NPC style text to a level. 
These can be placed anywhere you like. Like most objects, these have 
properties that you can tweak and customize to your heart's content;
	
Dialogue - the text a dialogue trigger will use when actively talking with it.
 It is worth noting that this property is modified in a submenu. 
A quick description of what every button does:
	
Remove - Removes the last page from the dialogue
Add - Adds a page to the end of the dialogue
Switch to - ID of the dialogue object to switch to when finishing the page
Expressions - click the head to cycle through the expressions (NPCs only)
Actions - click the body to cycle through actions to perform 
on that page of dialogue (NPCs only)
Responses - click Mario to cycle through reactions for the player 
to display after that page of dialogue

Bubble Text - text that appears overhead when the player is nearby
Tag - ID of this dialogue object, similar to water/lava
Delegate Tag - Will start dialogue from the specified object ID instead
Zoom - Will specify the zoom amount when focused on the object

--NPCs--
NPCs are objects specifically designed
for dialogue objects. When dialogue is 
placed on top of them, the dialogue will
attach itself to the NPC when playing.
Their properties are as follows;
	
Idle Expression/Action - expression/action when idling
Speaking Expression/Action* - action when idling/speaking 
Tag Link - links a dialogue trigger to the NPC from a distance (uses Tag)
Path Options - properties like custom path, walk speed, physics enabled, 
and move type. Each are fairly self explanatory.
Path Reference - Gives a visual on where the NPC's path is located
*require an attached dialogue trigger with bubble text

--Signs--
Signs act as single page NPCs that
cannot show emotion. These are best
used as, well, signs. There's nothing
very noteworthy to bring up
so properties won't be discussed here,
as they're self explanatory.

If anything above isn't clear or you still have questions, 
feel free to ask in the Super Mario 127 Discord!
"
